            "bodyHtml": "<p>Complete the notes below. Write <strong>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</strong> for each answer.</p><div><div><strong>Study of Fossil Park</strong></div><p>Types of fossils:</p><ul><li>transitional fossils: rare, show evidence of evolutionary change</li><li>{{31}} fossils: more common, actual fossilised remains</li><li>{{32}} fossils: indirect evidence of animals, such as footprints or tunnels</li></ul><p>Fossilisation processes:</p><ul><li>Organism trapped in volcanic ash</li><li>Petrifaction:</li><li>An animal is {{33}} in the mud after death</li><li>Mud dries and hardens</li><li>{{34}} replace the bones, leaving a stone shape</li></ul><p>Purchasing fossils:</p><ul><li>Site: shop outside the park, or from the park's {{35}}</li><li>Prices: generally {{36}}</li></ul></div>",
